IMPORT prelude

-- Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013 (NSW) -- the provisions a person bringing or answering a claim in the
-- NSW Civil and Administrative Tribunal (NCAT) meets: jurisdiction (Part 3), federal matters (Part 3A), practice and
-- procedure (Part 4 Divisions 2-5), enforcing and contravening orders (Part 5, with s 71), appeals (Part 6), and the claims machinery of the
-- Division Schedules (Schedule 3 clauses 9, 12-13, 13B, 15-18; Schedule 4 clauses 5, 7, 8, 10, 12; Schedule 5 clauses 27, 29;
-- Schedule 6 clauses 6, 9, 11, 12, 14).
--
-- SEAT: the party to proceedings in the Tribunal: usually the applicant (a tenant, consumer, home owner, retail lessee,
-- discrimination complainant, person seeking review of a government decision such as a victims support decision), and
-- on appeal the appellant; a respondent who answers the claim asks the same questions of the same rules. Every exported
-- question is one that party would ask: "Is my application in time?", "Can I have a lawyer?", "Can I be ordered to pay
-- costs?", "By when must I ask for reasons?", "Can I appeal, and do I need leave?", "How do I enforce my order?". The
-- Tribunal, its registrars, the President and the courts get no seat: what they must or may do is encoded as what it
-- means for the party.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "only if", "where", "unless" or "except", a flat "does not"/"may not"/"cannot", a period
-- fixed in the Act's own words), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a
-- "NOTHING-kind" comment. A judgment the Act leaves to the Tribunal or a court ("considers", "is satisfied", "special
-- circumstances", "reasonable explanation", "at its discretion") is asked as an input and the answer is conditional on
-- it; it is never decided here.
--
-- TIME. "within 28 days of being given notice", "within 12 months after the end of the period", "within the period of
-- 12 months of the date" are counted excluding the first day (the Interpretation Act 1987 s 36(1), not deposited), so the
-- last day is the day 28 days, or the same day of the month 12 or 24 months, after it (fork F2). The Interpretation Act's
-- move of a last day falling on a weekend or holiday (s 36(2)) is not applied (fork F3). Dates use only the prelude's
-- built-in DATE functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL), not daydate.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; corpus document dated 1 July 2024; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING.
-- Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013 -- a party's claim in NCAT`

§§ `The nouns`

-- ss 28-33: the four kinds of jurisdiction (appeal jurisdiction split into external and internal, s 28(2)(c)).
DECLARE `Kind of jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    `general jurisdiction (s 29)`
    `administrative review jurisdiction (s 30)`
    `external appeal jurisdiction (s 31)`

-- s 16(1): the Divisions. "Appeal Panel" stands for an internal appeal, which s 16(4) allocates to no Division.
DECLARE `NCAT Division` IS ONE OF
    `the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division`
    `the Consumer and Commercial Division`
    `the Occupational Division`
    `the Guardianship Division`

-- s 40 with s 41: the answer to "is my application in time?".
DECLARE `My application's timing` IS ONE OF
    `my application is in time`
    `my application is late, but the Tribunal may still extend the time even though it has expired`

-- s 43, s 83(5), Sch 3 cl 17(3), 18(2), Sch 5 cl 29(9), Sch 6 cl 14(5): what I have lodged against a decision.
DECLARE `What I have lodged` IS ONE OF
    `a general application to review a decision of someone outside the Tribunal`
    `an external appeal to the Tribunal`
    `an internal appeal to the Appeal Panel`
    `an administrative review application`
    `an appeal to a court under Part 6 Division 3`
    `an appeal to a court under Schedule 3 clause 17 or 18 or Schedule 5 clause 29`
    `an appeal to the Supreme Court from the Guardianship Division under Schedule 6 clause 14`

DECLARE `Order about the decision` IS ONE OF
    `no order has been made`
    `an order staying the decision, or otherwise stopping it operating`
    `an order letting the decision operate while the appeal is pending`

-- s 45 with the Division Schedules: who would represent me.
DECLARE `My representative` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian legal practitioner`
    `another person who is not a practising lawyer`

DECLARE `My representation` IS ONE OF
    `I am entitled to be represented by that person without the Tribunal's leave`
    `I may be represented by that person, because the Tribunal has granted leave`
    `I may be represented by that person only if the Tribunal grants leave; otherwise I conduct my own case`

-- s 50, Sch 6 cl 6.
DECLARE `What the step is for` IS ONE OF
    `deciding whether to grant leave for an external or internal appeal`
    `a resolution process, such as conciliation or mediation`
    `deciding the matter itself`

DECLARE `My hearing` IS ONE OF
    `a hearing is required`
    `no hearing is required`
    `no hearing is required, but the order dispensing with it was made without first hearing from the parties, which is an irregularity the Tribunal may set aside`

-- s 55(1), Sch 4 cl 10(2)(a).
DECLARE `What has happened in my proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `I withdrew my application or appeal`
    `the Tribunal considers my proceedings frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance`
    `I failed to appear`
    `the Tribunal considers there has been a want of prosecution`
    `none of these`

-- Sch 4 cl 10.
DECLARE `Who is causing the disadvantage` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `a party other than the applicant`

DECLARE `Disadvantage powers` IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal may dismiss or strike out the proceedings, or part of them`
    `the Tribunal may decide the proceedings, or part of them, in the applicant's favour, or strike the other party out`
    `clause 10 does not apply`

-- s 59.
DECLARE `My settlement` IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal may make orders giving effect to the settlement`
    `the Tribunal may dismiss the application or appeal, because it is not satisfied it could decide in those terms`
    `section 59 does not apply until the terms are in writing, signed by or for the parties and lodged`

-- s 60, Sch 3 cl 12, 13.
DECLARE `Proceedings for costs` IS ONE OF
    `a Working with Children decision (Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012)`
    `an NDIS worker check decision (National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Checks) Act 2018)`
    `an administrative review of a victims support decision (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013)`
    `proceedings under the Dormant Funds Act 1942`
    `any other proceedings`

DECLARE `My costs` IS ONE OF
    `each party pays its own costs, and the Tribunal may not award costs`
    `each party pays its own costs: costs can be awarded only for special circumstances, and the Tribunal is not satisfied there are any`
    `costs may be awarded because the Tribunal is satisfied there are special circumstances; it decides who pays and how much`
    `costs are in the Tribunal's discretion`

-- s 61.
DECLARE `Kind of decision taking effect` IS ONE OF
    `a general decision`
    `a decision determining an external or internal appeal`
    `an administrative review decision`

-- s 62(2A).
DECLARE `Kind of decision for reasons` IS ONE OF
    `a decision dispensing with a hearing under section 50(2)`
    `a decision to grant an adjournment`
    `a decision not to award costs`
    `a decision to award costs in the Consumer and Commercial Division, or in an internal appeal from it`
    `an order made with the consent of the parties`
    `a minor procedural decision with no final or determinative effect on my rights`
    `any other decision`

DECLARE `My right to reasons` IS ONE OF
    `I may request a written statement of reasons within 28 days of being given notice of the decision`
    `a written statement of reasons has already been provided to me`
    `section 62(2) gives no right to request reasons for this kind of decision`

-- Sch 6 cl 11(2).
DECLARE `Guardianship decision` IS ONE OF
    `a decision about consent to minor treatment (Guardianship Act 1987 s 36)`
    `a decision under Part 5A of the Guardianship Act 1987 (reciprocal arrangements)`
    `an ancillary or interlocutory decision`
    `any other Guardianship Division decision`

DECLARE `My reasons from the Tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `the reasons were provided in time`
    `the reasons were not provided within 28 days after my request`
    `not yet provided, and the 28 days have not ended`

-- s 78.
DECLARE `Amount ordered` IS ONE OF
    `an amount that is not a penalty (including costs)`
    `a civil or other penalty under other legislation`

DECLARE `Enforcing my order` IS ONE OF
    `the registrar's certificate, filed in that court, operates as a judgment of that court for the amount`
    `have the amount certified by a registrar, identifying the person liable, and file the certificate in a court that can give judgment for that amount`
    `file the certificate in a court that can give judgment for a debt of that amount; this one cannot`
    `the penalty may be registered as a judgment debt in a court of competent jurisdiction and enforced accordingly`

-- Sch 4 cl 8.
DECLARE `My renewal` IS ONE OF
    `I may renew the proceedings by lodging the notice; it is treated as a new application`
    `the 12 months after the end of the compliance period have passed`
    `not yet: the period the Tribunal gave for compliance has not ended`
    `clause 8 does not apply: the order was complied with in time`
    `clause 8 does not apply: the order's operation was suspended, or it is or has been under internal appeal`
    `clause 8 does not apply: the Tribunal has not given me leave to renew`
    `clause 8 applies only to orders in the Consumer and Commercial Division`

-- ss 32, 80, Sch 3 cl 15-16, Sch 4 cl 12(2), Sch 5 cl 29(1), Sch 6 cl 12.
DECLARE `Who made the decision` IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal at first instance, in a general or administrative review matter`
    `the Tribunal imposing a civil penalty in its general jurisdiction`
    `a registrar, in a kind of decision declared internally appealable`
    `a registrar, in any other kind of decision`
    `an Appeal Panel`
    `the Tribunal in an external appeal`
    `the Tribunal in contempt or civil penalty enforcement proceedings under this Act`

DECLARE `Kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `an interlocutory decision`
    `a decision as to costs`
    `a decision made with the consent of the parties`
    `any other decision, ancillary or final`

DECLARE `My ground of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `a question of law`
    `other grounds (fact, or fact and law)`

DECLARE `Special kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `none of the special kinds`
    `a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision`
    `a decision under the lands legislation`
    `a Native Title (New South Wales) Act 1994 Part 7 determination`
    `a Plant Diseases Act 1924 s 21 administrative review decision`
    `a victims support administrative review decision under Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 51`
    `a decision on leave under Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 s 96`
    `an interim order under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1977`
    `a profession decision of the Occupational Division (Schedule 5 clause 29(1))`
    `a Consumer and Commercial credit dispute decision, appealed by a corporation (Credit (Commonwealth Powers) Act 2010 Sch 3)`
    `a tenancy termination order under which a warrant of possession has been executed`
    `a Guardianship Division decision I have already appealed to the Supreme Court`

DECLARE `My internal appeal` IS ONE OF
    `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel as of right`
    `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel only with its leave`
    `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel on a question of law only, as of right, and not on other grounds even with leave`
    `no internal appeal lies against this decision`
    `only a party to the proceedings in which the decision was made may appeal`

-- s 82, 83, Sch 3 cl 17-18, Sch 5 cl 29, Sch 6 cl 12, 14.
DECLARE `Decision for a court appeal` IS ONE OF
    `a decision of an Appeal Panel in an internal appeal from the Tribunal`
    `a decision of an Appeal Panel in an internal appeal from a registrar`
    `a decision of the Tribunal in an external appeal`
    `a decision in proceedings in which a civil penalty was imposed on me`
    `a decision in proceedings for contempt of the Tribunal`
    `a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division`
    `a lands legislation decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division`
    `a profession decision of the Occupational Division under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (NSW)`
    `any other profession decision of the Occupational Division`
    `an internally appealable decision of the Tribunal in the Guardianship Division`
    `a decision Schedule 3 clause 15 makes not internally appealable, with no court appeal given (victims support s 51 review, Native Title Part 7, Plant Diseases s 21, Anti-Discrimination Act s 96 leave)`
    `any other decision of the Tribunal at first instance`

DECLARE `My court appeal` IS ONE OF
    `to the Supreme Court, with its leave, on a question of law only`
    `to the Supreme Court, as of right, on a question of law`
    `to the District Court, as of right, on a question of law`
    `to the Supreme Court, as of right on a question of law, or with its leave on other grounds`
    `to the Supreme Court, only with its leave`
    `to the Supreme Court, by way of rehearing`
    `to the Land and Environment Court`
    `not on that ground: the appeal lies on a question of law only`
    `not under Part 6: a contempt decision is appealed under District Court Act 1973 s 201, as applied by section 73`
    `no appeal to a court lies under this Act against this decision`
    `not to a court under this Act: the decision goes first to an internal appeal`
    `not while my internal appeal stands, unless it is withdrawn with the Appeal Panel's approval`
    `only a party to the proceedings may appeal`

-- Part 3A.
DECLARE `My federal transfer` IS ONE OF
    `the court may grant leave for my application or appeal to be made to it instead of the Tribunal`
    `the court cannot grant leave on these facts`
    `the court cannot grant leave until the appeal already lodged is determined`

DECLARE `My substituted proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `taken to have started in the court on the day I first made it to the Tribunal, despite any limitation period`
    `taken to have started on the day I first made it to the Tribunal, but section 34C(2) does not save it from the limitation period`
    `section 34C applies only once the court grants leave`

-- The parties and acts of the regulative rules (ss 40, 62(2), 84(2), Sch 4 cl 8(2), Sch 6 cl 14(2)).
DECLARE `NCAT party` IS ONE OF `the party`, `the Tribunal`
DECLARE `NCAT act` IS ONE OF
    `lodge the application or appeal`
    `request a written statement of reasons`
    `provide the written statement of reasons`
    `lodge a notice renewing the proceedings`
    `institute the appeal to the court`

§§ `Dates`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` `days` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `days`)

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in the month of` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the first of the next month` MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day`))
    WHERE
        `the first of the next month` MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12
            THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)
            ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `the day`)

-- READING (fork F2): a period of months "after" or "of" a day ends on the same day of the month that many months later,
-- or on that month's last day where it is shorter (29 February 2028 to 28 February 2029).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus months` `months` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the smaller day` `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `months from year zero` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day`) TIMES 12 PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `months`
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`months from year zero` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS `months from year zero` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12) PLUS 1
        `the smaller day` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the number of days in the month of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `the month` `the year`)
            THEN DATE_DAY `the day`
            ELSE `the number of days in the month of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `the month` `the year`)


GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

§§ `Part 3 -- jurisdiction`

-- s 28(1) "The Tribunal has such jurisdiction and functions as may be conferred or imposed on it by or under this Act or
-- any other legislation." s 29(1): general jurisdiction where legislation "enables the Tribunal to make decisions ... in
-- respect of that matter" and the matter "does not otherwise fall within" the other kinds. s 30: administrative review
-- jurisdiction is given by the Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 (not deposited: asked). s 31(1): external appeal
-- jurisdiction "if legislation provides that an appeal may be made to the Tribunal". Internal appeals are asked under
-- Part 6 below; enforcement jurisdiction (s 33) is begun only by an authorised official (s 75), never by the party.
-- Where no legislation confers jurisdiction, s 28(1) is a grant limited in its own wording: NOTHING. The Act gives no
-- order between s 30 and s 31 where both could apply; external appeal is taken first (fork F1).
@export Which kind of NCAT jurisdiction does my application or appeal fall in (ss 28-31)?
GIVEN `legislation provides that an appeal may be made to the Tribunal against the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Act or regulation says the decision you are challenging (made by someone outside the Tribunal) can be appealed to NCAT
      `the Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 gives the Tribunal review of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is one of a government administrator that the Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 makes reviewable by NCAT (an "administratively reviewable decision")
      `legislation lets the Tribunal decide the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Act or regulation (other than the NCAT Act and its rules) lets NCAT make decisions about your matter, for example a tenancy, consumer, home building or discrimination claim
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of jurisdiction`
`Which kind of jurisdiction is my matter in` MEANS
    IF `legislation provides that an appeal may be made to the Tribunal against the decision`
    THEN JUST `external appeal jurisdiction (s 31)`
    ELSE IF `the Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 gives the Tribunal review of the decision`
         THEN JUST `administrative review jurisdiction (s 30)`
         ELSE IF `legislation lets the Tribunal decide the matter`
              THEN JUST `general jurisdiction (s 29)`
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (grant limited in its own wording: s 28(1) gives only conferred jurisdiction)

§§ `Part 3A -- federal matters taken to a court`

-- s 34B(1) "A person with standing to make an original application or external appeal may, with the leave of an
-- authorised court [the District Court or the Local Court], make the application or appeal to the court instead of the
-- Tribunal." (2) "may grant leave ... only if it is satisfied that-- (a) the application or appeal was first made with
-- the Tribunal, and (b) the determination ... by the Tribunal would involve an exercise of federal jurisdiction, and (c)
-- the Tribunal would otherwise have had original jurisdiction or external appellate jurisdiction ..., and (d) substituted
-- proceedings ... would be within the jurisdictional limit of the court." (4)(a): an appeal lodged before the application
-- for leave: "the court cannot grant leave unless and until the appeal is determined". "only if": JUST FALSE-like answer
-- when a condition fails. Whether federal jurisdiction is involved (for example, parties resident in different States)
-- is asked. The court's satisfaction is answered as the facts given.
@export Can I take my NCAT application or appeal to the District Court or Local Court instead, because it involves federal jurisdiction (s 34B)?
GIVEN `I have standing to make the application or external appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person entitled to make the application, or the external appeal, to NCAT in the first place
      `I first made the application or appeal to the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you first lodged the application or appeal with NCAT
      `deciding it would involve federal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT deciding it would involve federal jurisdiction (for example, because you and the other party live in different States, or a party is the Commonwealth)
      `the Tribunal would otherwise have jurisdiction to decide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT would have had jurisdiction to decide the application or external appeal, if federal jurisdiction were not involved
      `it is within the court's jurisdictional limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is within the money limit of the court you apply to (the District Court or the Local Court), as the Civil Procedure Act 2005 sets it
      `an appeal about a matter in issue was lodged before I applied for leave and is not yet determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an appeal under the NCAT Act about a matter in issue was lodged before you applied to the court for leave, and has not yet been decided
GIVETH A `My federal transfer`
`Can I take my matter to a court instead` MEANS
    IF     `I have standing to make the application or external appeal`
       AND `I first made the application or appeal to the Tribunal`
       AND `deciding it would involve federal jurisdiction`
       AND `the Tribunal would otherwise have jurisdiction to decide it`
       AND `it is within the court's jurisdictional limit`
    THEN IF `an appeal about a matter in issue was lodged before I applied for leave and is not yet determined`
         THEN `the court cannot grant leave until the appeal already lodged is determined`
         ELSE `the court may grant leave for my application or appeal to be made to it instead of the Tribunal`
    ELSE `the court cannot grant leave on these facts`

-- s 34C(1)(a): substituted proceedings "are taken to have been commenced in the authorised court on the day on which the
-- application or appeal was first made to the Tribunal". (2) "Subsection (1) applies despite any limitation period ...
-- provided it was first lodged with the Tribunal before the expiry of the period." A period expires at the end of its last
-- day, so lodging on the last day is before its expiry (fork F4).
@export If the court gives leave, on what footing are my court proceedings taken to have started, given my time limit (s 34C)?
GIVEN `the court has granted leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the District Court or Local Court has granted leave under s 34B for your application or appeal to be made to it
      `the day I first lodged it with the Tribunal` IS A DATE @desc The day you first lodged the application or appeal with NCAT
      `the last day of my limitation period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the limitation period (under the Limitation Act 1969 or the Act you claim under) for your application or appeal
GIVETH A `My substituted proceedings`
`How my court proceedings are taken to have started` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the court has granted leave`)
    THEN `section 34C applies only once the court grants leave`
    ELSE IF `the day I first lodged it with the Tribunal` `is after` `the last day of my limitation period`
         THEN `taken to have started on the day I first made it to the Tribunal, but section 34C(2) does not save it from the limitation period`
         ELSE `taken to have started in the court on the day I first made it to the Tribunal, despite any limitation period`

§§ `Part 4 Division 2 -- starting proceedings`

-- s 40 "An application or appeal to the Tribunal is to be made in the time and manner prescribed by enabling legislation
-- or the procedural rules." s 41(1) "The Tribunal may ... extend the period of time for the doing of anything under any
-- legislation in respect of which the Tribunal has jurisdiction despite anything to the contrary under that legislation."
-- (2) "Such an application may be made even though the relevant period of time has expired." Neither the enabling Acts
-- nor the NCAT Rules are deposited: the last day is asked. Whether to extend is the Tribunal's discretion: asked.
GIVEN `the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NCAT party` `NCAT act`
`s 40 -- an application or appeal must be made in the time prescribed` `the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the party`
    MUST `lodge the application or appeal`
    WITHIN `the last day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the party` BECAUSE "application or appeal not made within the time prescribed by the enabling legislation or the procedural rules, as extended (ss 40, 41)"

@export Is my application or appeal to NCAT in time, and if it is late can the time still be extended (ss 40, 41)?
GIVEN `the last day prescribed` IS A DATE @desc The last day for making your application or appeal, as the Act you apply under or the NCAT Rules set it
      `the Tribunal has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT has already extended the time for your application or appeal
      `the last day as extended` IS A DATE @desc If NCAT extended the time, the new last day (otherwise any date)
      `the day I lodge` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge (or lodged) your application or appeal
GIVETH A `My application's timing`
`Is my application in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- an application or appeal must be made in the time prescribed` `the last day`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day lodged`), (EVENT `the party` `lodge the application or appeal` `the day lodged`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN `my application is in time`
    OTHERWISE `my application is late, but the Tribunal may still extend the time even though it has expired`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `the Tribunal has extended the time`
            THEN DATE_SERIAL `the last day as extended`
            ELSE DATE_SERIAL `the last day prescribed`
        `the day lodged` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day I lodge`

-- s 43(2) "A pending general application or appeal does not affect the operation of the decision ... unless the Tribunal
-- makes an order staying or otherwise affecting the operation of the decision." It covers a general application to
-- review a decision of an external decision-maker, an external appeal and an internal appeal (s 43(1)). s 83(5), Sch 3
-- cl 17(3), 18(2) and Sch 5 cl 29(9): an appeal to a court "does not affect the operation" of the decision, "subject to
-- any interlocutory order". Sch 6 cl 14(5): an appeal to the Supreme Court from the Guardianship Division "operates to
-- stay the decision", subject to any interlocutory order. An administrative review application is governed by the
-- Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 (s 43 note), not deposited: NOTHING.
@export Does my application or appeal stop the decision I am challenging from operating meanwhile (s 43, s 83(5), Schedules 3, 5 and 6)?
GIVEN `what I have lodged` IS A `What I have lodged` @desc What you have lodged. One of: "a general application to review a decision of someone outside the Tribunal", "an external appeal to the Tribunal", "an internal appeal to the Appeal Panel", "an administrative review application", "an appeal to a court under Part 6 Division 3", "an appeal to a court under Schedule 3 clause 17 or 18 or Schedule 5 clause 29", "an appeal to the Supreme Court from the Guardianship Division under Schedule 6 clause 14"
      `the order made about the decision` IS AN `Order about the decision` @desc Any order NCAT or the court has made about the decision meanwhile. One of: "no order has been made", "an order staying the decision, or otherwise stopping it operating", "an order letting the decision operate while the appeal is pending"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my challenge stop the decision` MEANS
    IF `what I have lodged` EQUALS `an administrative review application`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 Ch 3 Pt 3 Div 2)
    ELSE IF `what I have lodged` EQUALS `an appeal to the Supreme Court from the Guardianship Division under Schedule 6 clause 14`
         THEN IF `the order made about the decision` EQUALS `an order letting the decision operate while the appeal is pending`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the order made about the decision` EQUALS `an order staying the decision, or otherwise stopping it operating`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 4 Division 3 -- representation`

-- s 45(1) "A party ... (a) has the carriage of the party's own case and is not entitled to be represented by any person,
-- and (b) may be represented by another person only if the Tribunal grants leave". (2) In an internal appeal a party may
-- be represented without leave "if the party was entitled to be represented by such a person without the leave of
-- Tribunal in the proceedings in which the decision under appeal was made": so the Division below is the input. The
-- Division Schedules entitle a party without leave: Sch 3 cl 9(1) and Sch 5 cl 27 (an Australian legal practitioner, in
-- every Administrative and Equal Opportunity or Occupational Division matter); Sch 4 cl 7(a) (an Australian legal
-- practitioner, where the party has legal assistance under the Fair Trading Act 1987) and (b) ("an Australian lawyer or
-- other agent", in Retail Leases Act 1994 matters: read as any representative, fork F5); Sch 6 cl 9 (an Australian legal
-- practitioner, in Children and Young Persons (Care and Protection) Act 1998 s 175 matters). "only if": the third answer.
@export Can I be represented in my NCAT proceedings by a lawyer or another person, and do I need the Tribunal's leave (s 45 and the Division Schedules)?
GIVEN `the Division` IS AN `NCAT Division` @desc The Division of NCAT your proceedings are in; for an internal appeal, the Division the decision under appeal was made in. One of: "the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division" (discrimination, reviews of government decisions such as victims support), "the Consumer and Commercial Division" (tenancy, consumer, home building, strata, retail leases), "the Occupational Division", "the Guardianship Division"
      `my representative` IS A `My representative` @desc Who would represent you. One of: "an Australian legal practitioner" (a lawyer with a practising certificate), "another person who is not a practising lawyer" (a friend, relative, advocate or agent)
      `I have been granted legal assistance under the Fair Trading Act 1987` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been granted legal assistance under Division 2 of Part 2 of the Fair Trading Act 1987 for these proceedings
      `the proceedings are under the Retail Leases Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceedings are a retail lease dispute under the Retail Leases Act 1994
      `the proceedings are about special medical treatment of a child under the care and protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceedings are about special medical treatment of a child under section 175 of the Children and Young Persons (Care and Protection) Act 1998
      `the Tribunal has granted leave for that person to represent me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT (or the Appeal Panel) has granted leave for that person to represent you, and has not revoked it
GIVETH A `My representation`
`Can I be represented` MEANS
    IF `entitled without leave`
    THEN `I am entitled to be represented by that person without the Tribunal's leave`
    ELSE IF `the Tribunal has granted leave for that person to represent me`
         THEN `I may be represented by that person, because the Tribunal has granted leave`
         ELSE `I may be represented by that person only if the Tribunal grants leave; otherwise I conduct my own case`
    WHERE
        `a practitioner` MEANS `my representative` EQUALS `an Australian legal practitioner`
        `entitled without leave` MEANS
                (`the Division` EQUALS `the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division` AND `a practitioner`)
             OR (`the Division` EQUALS `the Occupational Division` AND `a practitioner`)
             OR (`the Division` EQUALS `the Consumer and Commercial Division` AND `the proceedings are under the Retail Leases Act 1994`)
             OR (`the Division` EQUALS `the Consumer and Commercial Division` AND `I have been granted legal assistance under the Fair Trading Act 1987` AND `a practitioner`)
             OR (`the Division` EQUALS `the Guardianship Division` AND `the proceedings are about special medical treatment of a child under the care and protection Act` AND `a practitioner`)

§§ `Part 4 Division 4 -- hearings and dismissal`

-- s 50(1) "A hearing is required for proceedings in the Tribunal except-- (a) in proceedings for the granting of leave
-- for an external or internal appeal, or (b) in connection with the use of any resolution processes ..., or (c) if the
-- Tribunal makes an order under this section dispensing with a hearing, or (d) in such other circumstances as may be
-- prescribed by the procedural rules." (3) "The Tribunal may not make an order dispensing with a hearing unless the
-- Tribunal has first-- (a) afforded the parties an opportunity to make submissions ..., and (b) taken any such
-- submissions into account." s 53(3): a failure to comply with the Act "is to be treated as an irregularity and does not
-- nullify the proceedings or any decision ... unless the Tribunal determines otherwise"; (4) the Tribunal may set it
-- aside (fork F6). Sch 6 cl 6(1): "Despite section 50 ..., the Tribunal is required to hold a hearing in proceedings that
-- involve the exercise of a substantive Division function" (Guardianship).
@export Must there be a hearing of my proceedings, or can NCAT decide on the papers (s 50, Schedule 6 clause 6)?
GIVEN `what the step is for` IS A `What the step is for` @desc What is being decided. One of: "deciding whether to grant leave for an external or internal appeal", "a resolution process, such as conciliation or mediation", "deciding the matter itself"
      `the proceedings are in the Guardianship Division and involve a substantive Division function` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceedings are in the Guardianship Division and involve deciding the matter itself (not just an ancillary or interlocutory decision)
      `the procedural rules dispense with a hearing in this kind of case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the NCAT Rules or regulations say no hearing is needed in a case like yours
      `the Tribunal has ordered that the hearing be dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT has made an order dispensing with a hearing
      `the parties were first given an opportunity to make submissions about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before making that order, NCAT gave the parties a chance to make submissions about dispensing with the hearing and took them into account
GIVETH A `My hearing`
`Must there be a hearing` MEANS
    IF `what the step is for` EQUALS `deciding whether to grant leave for an external or internal appeal`
    THEN `no hearing is required`
    ELSE IF `the proceedings are in the Guardianship Division and involve a substantive Division function`
         THEN `a hearing is required`
         ELSE IF `what the step is for` EQUALS `a resolution process, such as conciliation or mediation`
              THEN `no hearing is required`
              ELSE IF `the procedural rules dispense with a hearing in this kind of case`
                   THEN `no hearing is required`
                   ELSE IF `the Tribunal has ordered that the hearing be dispensed with`
                        THEN IF `the parties were first given an opportunity to make submissions about it`
                             THEN `no hearing is required`
                             ELSE `no hearing is required, but the order dispensing with it was made without first hearing from the parties, which is an irregularity the Tribunal may set aside`
                        ELSE `a hearing is required`

-- s 55(1) "The Tribunal may dismiss at any stage any proceedings before it in any of the following circumstances-- (a) if
-- the applicant or appellant (or, if there is more than one ..., each applicant or appellant) withdraws ..., (b) if the
-- Tribunal considers that the proceedings are frivolous or vexatious or otherwise misconceived or lacking in substance,
-- (c) if the applicant or appellant (or ... each ...) has failed to appear ..., (d) if the Tribunal considers that there
-- has been a want of prosecution". Sch 4 cl 10(2)(a): in the Consumer and Commercial Division, if the applicant is
-- unreasonably disadvantaging another party, the proceedings may be dismissed or struck out. The list in s 55 is not
-- closed by "only" and other powers exist (s 59(2), Sch 4 cl 10): outside the grounds, NOTHING.
@export Can NCAT dismiss my application or appeal (s 55(1), Schedule 4 clause 10)?
GIVEN `what has happened` IS A `What has happened in my proceedings` @desc What has happened. One of: "I withdrew my application or appeal", "the Tribunal considers my proceedings frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance", "I failed to appear", "the Tribunal considers there has been a want of prosecution", "none of these"
      `every applicant or appellant has done the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where you withdrew or failed to appear: whether every applicant or appellant did so too (answer yes if you are the only one)
      `the Tribunal considers I am unreasonably disadvantaging another party in a Consumer and Commercial Division matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the applicant in the Consumer and Commercial Division and NCAT is of the opinion that you are conducting the proceedings in a way that unreasonably disadvantages another party (for example by not following its directions)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my application be dismissed` MEANS
    IF `the Tribunal considers I am unreasonably disadvantaging another party in a Consumer and Commercial Division matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF    `what has happened` EQUALS `the Tribunal considers my proceedings frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance`
            OR `what has happened` EQUALS `the Tribunal considers there has been a want of prosecution`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF    `what has happened` EQUALS `I withdrew my application or appeal`
                 OR `what has happened` EQUALS `I failed to appear`
              THEN IF `every applicant or appellant has done the same`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (grant limited in its own wording: s 55(1)(a), (c) need each applicant)
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the list in s 55(1) is not closed by "only")

-- s 55(2) "The Tribunal may reinstate proceedings that have been dismissed under subsection (1)(c) if the Tribunal
-- considers that there is a reasonable explanation for that failure." An "if": JUST FALSE without the explanation.
-- Proceedings dismissed on another ground: s 55(2) is silent (NOTHING).
@export My proceedings were dismissed because I did not appear: can they be reinstated (s 55(2))?
GIVEN `my proceedings were dismissed because I failed to appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT dismissed your proceedings because you (and any other applicant or appellant) failed to appear
      `the Tribunal considers there is a reasonable explanation for my failure to appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT accepts that there is a reasonable explanation for your not appearing (NCAT decides; answer as you expect it to)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my dismissed proceedings be reinstated` MEANS
    IF `my proceedings were dismissed because I failed to appear`
    THEN IF `the Tribunal considers there is a reasonable explanation for my failure to appear`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 55(2) speaks only of a dismissal under s 55(1)(c))

-- Sch 4 cl 10(1) "if the Tribunal is of the opinion that a party ... is conducting the proceedings in such a way that
-- unreasonably disadvantages another party ...". (2) "(a) if the party causing the disadvantage is the applicant--order
-- that the proceedings (or part ...) be dismissed or struck out, or (b) if the party causing the disadvantage is not the
-- applicant--(i) determine the proceedings (or part ...) in favour of the applicant and make any appropriate orders, or
-- (ii) order that the party causing the disadvantage be struck out". (3) lists matters the Tribunal must have regard to
-- first (familiarity, capacity, disability, deliberateness): left to the Tribunal.
@export In the Consumer and Commercial Division, what can NCAT do if a party is unreasonably disadvantaging another (Schedule 4 clause 10)?
GIVEN `the proceedings are in the Consumer and Commercial Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceedings are in NCAT's Consumer and Commercial Division (tenancy, consumer, home building, strata and similar)
      `the Tribunal is of the opinion that a party is unreasonably disadvantaging another party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT is of the opinion that a party is conducting the proceedings in a way that unreasonably disadvantages another party, including by not complying with its orders or directions
      `who is causing the disadvantage` IS A `Who is causing the disadvantage` @desc Who is causing the disadvantage. One of: "the applicant", "a party other than the applicant"
GIVETH A `Disadvantage powers`
`What can be done about a party causing disadvantage` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in the Consumer and Commercial Division` AND `the Tribunal is of the opinion that a party is unreasonably disadvantaging another party`
    THEN IF `who is causing the disadvantage` EQUALS `the applicant`
         THEN `the Tribunal may dismiss or strike out the proceedings, or part of them`
         ELSE `the Tribunal may decide the proceedings, or part of them, in the applicant's favour, or strike the other party out`
    ELSE `clause 10 does not apply`

§§ `Part 4 Division 5 -- settlement, costs, decisions and reasons`

-- s 59(1) the Tribunal may make orders "to give effect to any agreed settlement ... if-- (a) the terms of the agreed
-- settlement are in writing, signed by or on behalf of the parties and lodged with the Tribunal, and (b) the Tribunal is
-- satisfied that it would have the power to make a decision in the terms of the agreed settlement or in terms that are
-- consistent with" them. (2) If not so satisfied it may dismiss the application or appeal.
@export Can NCAT make orders to give effect to the settlement we have agreed (s 59)?
GIVEN `the terms are in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms of your settlement are in writing
      `the terms are signed by or on behalf of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the written terms are signed by or on behalf of every party
      `the terms are lodged with the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the signed terms have been lodged with NCAT
      `the Tribunal is satisfied it could make a decision in those terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT is satisfied that it would have power to make a decision in the terms of the settlement, or consistent with them (NCAT decides; answer as you expect it to)
GIVETH A `My settlement`
`Can our settlement be made into orders` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the terms are in writing` AND `the terms are signed by or on behalf of the parties` AND `the terms are lodged with the Tribunal`))
    THEN `section 59 does not apply until the terms are in writing, signed by or for the parties and lodged`
    ELSE IF `the Tribunal is satisfied it could make a decision in those terms`
         THEN `the Tribunal may make orders giving effect to the settlement`
         ELSE `the Tribunal may dismiss the application or appeal, because it is not satisfied it could decide in those terms`

-- s 60(1) "Each party to proceedings in the Tribunal is to pay the party's own costs." (2) "The Tribunal may award costs
-- ... only if it is satisfied that there are special circumstances warranting an award of costs." (3) lists matters it
-- may have regard to: left to the Tribunal (the "special circumstances" input). Sch 3 cl 13: "Despite section 60 ..., the
-- Tribunal may not award costs" in Working with Children, NDIS worker check, and Victims Rights and Support Act 2013
-- administrative review proceedings. Sch 3 cl 12(1): "Despite section 60(1) and (2) ..., the Tribunal may, in its
-- discretion, award costs" in Dormant Funds Act 1942 proceedings. s 35 makes s 60 subject to enabling legislation and the
-- procedural rules (not deposited); see NOTES.md finding 2.
@export Will I have to pay my own costs in NCAT, and can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs or get mine paid (s 60, Schedule 3 clauses 12 and 13)?
GIVEN `the proceedings` IS A `Proceedings for costs` @desc What the proceedings are. One of: "a Working with Children decision (Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012)", "an NDIS worker check decision (National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Checks) Act 2018)", "an administrative review of a victims support decision (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013)", "proceedings under the Dormant Funds Act 1942", "any other proceedings"
      `the Tribunal is satisfied there are special circumstances warranting costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT is satisfied there are special circumstances warranting an award of costs, for example a party unnecessarily disadvantaging another, unreasonably prolonging the case, making a claim with no tenable basis, or not co-operating (NCAT decides; answer as you expect it to)
GIVETH A `My costs`
`Who pays the costs` MEANS
    IF    `the proceedings` EQUALS `a Working with Children decision (Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012)`
       OR `the proceedings` EQUALS `an NDIS worker check decision (National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Checks) Act 2018)`
       OR `the proceedings` EQUALS `an administrative review of a victims support decision (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013)`
    THEN `each party pays its own costs, and the Tribunal may not award costs`
    ELSE IF `the proceedings` EQUALS `proceedings under the Dormant Funds Act 1942`
         THEN `costs are in the Tribunal's discretion`
         ELSE IF `the Tribunal is satisfied there are special circumstances warranting costs`
              THEN `costs may be awarded because the Tribunal is satisfied there are special circumstances; it decides who pays and how much`
              ELSE `each party pays its own costs: costs can be awarded only for special circumstances, and the Tribunal is not satisfied there are any`

-- s 61 "A general decision or a decision determining an external or internal appeal takes effect on the date on which it
-- is given or such later date as may be specified in the decision." An administrative review decision takes effect under
-- Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 s 66 (the note), not deposited: NOTHING.
@export On what date does NCAT's decision in my proceedings take effect (s 61)?
GIVEN `the kind of decision` IS A `Kind of decision taking effect` @desc What kind of decision it is. One of: "a general decision" (for example on a tenancy, consumer or discrimination claim), "a decision determining an external or internal appeal", "an administrative review decision"
      `the date the decision was given` IS A DATE @desc The date NCAT gave the decision
      `the decision specifies a later date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision says it takes effect on a later date
      `the later date specified` IS A DATE @desc The later date the decision specifies (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`When does the decision take effect` MEANS
    IF `the kind of decision` EQUALS `an administrative review decision`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: Administrative Decisions Review Act 1997 s 66)
    ELSE IF `the decision specifies a later date` AND `the later date specified` `is after` `the date the decision was given`
         THEN JUST `the later date specified`
         ELSE JUST `the date the decision was given`

-- s 62(2) "Any party may, within 28 days of being given notice of a decision of the Tribunal, request the Tribunal to
-- provide a written statement of reasons for its decision if a written statement of reasons has not already been
-- provided to the party." (2A) "Subsection (2) does not apply to" (a) dispensing with a hearing, (b) an adjournment,
-- (c) "a decision under section 60 not to award costs, except where a party has argued there are special circumstances",
-- (d) a decision to award costs in Consumer and Commercial Division proceedings or an internal appeal from them, (e) an
-- order made by consent, (f) "other minor procedural decisions that do not have a final or determinative impact on the
-- rights of a party". A flat "does not apply": the third answer.
@export Can I ask NCAT for a written statement of reasons for its decision (s 62(2), (2A))?
GIVEN `the kind of decision` IS A `Kind of decision for reasons` @desc What kind of decision it is. One of: "a decision dispensing with a hearing under section 50(2)", "a decision to grant an adjournment", "a decision not to award costs", "a decision to award costs in the Consumer and Commercial Division, or in an internal appeal from it", "an order made with the consent of the parties", "a minor procedural decision with no final or determinative effect on my rights", "any other decision"
      `a party argued there were special circumstances warranting costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a decision not to award costs: whether a party argued that there were special circumstances warranting an award of costs
      `written reasons have already been provided to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT has already given you a written statement of reasons for this decision
GIVETH A `My right to reasons`
`Can I ask for reasons` MEANS
    IF `excluded by subsection (2A)`
    THEN `section 62(2) gives no right to request reasons for this kind of decision`
    ELSE IF `written reasons have already been provided to me`
         THEN `a written statement of reasons has already been provided to me`
         ELSE `I may request a written statement of reasons within 28 days of being given notice of the decision`
    WHERE
        `excluded by subsection (2A)` MEANS
               `the kind of decision` EQUALS `a decision dispensing with a hearing under section 50(2)`
            OR `the kind of decision` EQUALS `a decision to grant an adjournment`
            OR (`the kind of decision` EQUALS `a decision not to award costs` AND (NOT `a party argued there were special circumstances warranting costs`))
            OR `the kind of decision` EQUALS `a decision to award costs in the Consumer and Commercial Division, or in an internal appeal from it`
            OR `the kind of decision` EQUALS `an order made with the consent of the parties`
            OR `the kind of decision` EQUALS `a minor procedural decision with no final or determinative effect on my rights`

-- Sch 6 cl 11(1): in the Guardianship Division the Tribunal "must give each party ... a written statement of reasons for
-- any decision", subject to (2): it "is not required to provide a written statement of reasons for" minor treatment
-- consent decisions (s 36), Part 5A decisions and ancillary or interlocutory decisions "unless requested to do so by a
-- party under section 62". A flat "is not required": JUST FALSE for those kinds.
@export In the Guardianship Division, will I be given written reasons for the decision without having to ask (Schedule 6 clause 11)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Guardianship decision` @desc What kind of Guardianship Division decision it is. One of: "a decision about consent to minor treatment (Guardianship Act 1987 s 36)", "a decision under Part 5A of the Guardianship Act 1987 (reciprocal arrangements)", "an ancillary or interlocutory decision", "any other Guardianship Division decision"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Will I get guardianship reasons without asking` MEANS
    IF `the decision` EQUALS `any other Guardianship Division decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 62(2): the request is to be made "within 28 days of being given notice"; counted from the day after notice (fork F2).
@export What is the last day on which I can ask NCAT for written reasons for its decision (s 62(2))?
GIVEN `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of NCAT's decision
GIVETH A DATE
`The last day to ask for reasons` MEANS `the day I was given notice of the decision` `plus days` 28

GIVEN `the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NCAT party` `NCAT act`
`s 62(2) -- a party wanting reasons must request them within 28 days of notice` `the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the party`
    MUST `request a written statement of reasons`
    WITHIN `the last day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the party` BECAUSE "request for a written statement of reasons not made within 28 days of being given notice of the decision (s 62(2))"

@export Is my request to NCAT for written reasons in time (s 62(2))?
GIVEN `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of NCAT's decision
      `the day I made my request` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked NCAT for a written statement of reasons
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my request for reasons in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 62(2) -- a party wanting reasons must request them within 28 days of notice` `the last day`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day asked`), (EVENT `the party` `request a written statement of reasons` `the day asked`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (`The last day to ask for reasons` `the day I was given notice of the decision`)
        `the day asked` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day I made my request`

-- s 62(2) "The statement must be provided within 28 days after the request is made." The Tribunal's duty, encoded as
-- what the party must be given and by when.
@export By what day must NCAT give me the written reasons I asked for (s 62(2))?
GIVEN `the day I made my request` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked NCAT, in time, for a written statement of reasons
GIVETH A DATE
`The last day for the Tribunal to give me reasons` MEANS `the day I made my request` `plus days` 28

GIVEN `the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NCAT party` `NCAT act`
`s 62(2) -- the Tribunal must provide the statement within 28 days after the request` `the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the Tribunal`
    MUST `provide the written statement of reasons`
    WITHIN `the last day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the Tribunal` BECAUSE "written statement of reasons not provided within 28 days after the request (s 62(2))"

@export Has NCAT given me the written reasons I asked for within the 28 days (s 62(2))?
GIVEN `the day I made my request` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked NCAT, in time, for a written statement of reasons
      `the reasons have been provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT has given you the written statement of reasons
      `the day the reasons were provided` IS A DATE @desc The day NCAT gave you the written statement (otherwise any date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `My reasons from the Tribunal`
`Were my reasons given in time` MEANS
    IF `the reasons have been provided`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 62(2) -- the Tribunal must provide the statement within 28 days after the request` `the last day`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day provided`), (EVENT `the Tribunal` `provide the written statement of reasons` `the day provided`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the reasons were provided in time`
         OTHERWISE `the reasons were not provided within 28 days after my request`
    ELSE IF DATE_SERIAL `today` GREATER THAN `the last day`
         THEN `the reasons were not provided within 28 days after my request`
         ELSE `not yet provided, and the 28 days have not ended`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (`The last day for the Tribunal to give me reasons` `the day I made my request`)
        `the day provided` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day the reasons were provided`

§§ `Part 5 -- enforcing and contravening orders`

-- s 78(1) "For the purposes of the recovery of any amount ordered to be paid by the Tribunal (including costs, but not
-- including a civil or other penalty), the amount is to be certified by a registrar." (2) the certificate "must identify
-- the person liable". (3) a certificate given under (1) and "filed in the registry of a court having jurisdiction to give
-- judgment for a debt of the same amount ... operates as such a judgment". (4) "A civil or other penalty ordered to be
-- paid by the Tribunal (other than for a contravention of a civil penalty provision of this Act) may be registered as a
-- judgment debt in a court of competent jurisdiction and is enforceable accordingly." The courts' money limits are not in
-- the Act: asked.
@export How do I enforce an NCAT order that someone pay me money (s 78)?
GIVEN `what was ordered` IS AN `Amount ordered` @desc What NCAT ordered to be paid. One of: "an amount that is not a penalty (including costs)", "a civil or other penalty under other legislation"
      `a registrar has certified the amount, identifying the person liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an NCAT registrar has given a certificate of the amount that names the person who must pay
      `the court can give judgment for a debt of that amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court whose registry you file the certificate in can give judgment for a debt of that amount (for example the Local Court for smaller amounts)
GIVETH A `Enforcing my order`
`How do I enforce my money order` MEANS
    IF `what was ordered` EQUALS `a civil or other penalty under other legislation`
    THEN `the penalty may be registered as a judgment debt in a court of competent jurisdiction and enforced accordingly`
    ELSE IF (NOT `a registrar has certified the amount, identifying the person liable`)
         THEN `have the amount certified by a registrar, identifying the person liable, and file the certificate in a court that can give judgment for that amount`
         ELSE IF `the court can give judgment for a debt of that amount`
              THEN `the registrar's certificate, filed in that court, operates as a judgment of that court for the amount`
              ELSE `file the certificate in a court that can give judgment for a debt of that amount; this one cannot`

-- Sch 4 cl 8(1) the Tribunal "may ... give leave to the person in whose favour the order is made to renew the proceedings
-- if the order is not complied with within the period specified". (2) "If an order has not been complied with within the
-- period specified ..., the person in whose favour the order was made may renew the proceedings ... by lodging a notice
-- ..., within 12 months after the end of the period, stating that the order has not been complied with." (3) the notice is
-- treated as a new application. (5) "This clause does not apply if-- (a) the operation of an order has been suspended, or
-- (b) the order is or has been the subject of an internal appeal." Whether (2) needs the leave in (1) is not said; read
-- as needing it (fork F7).
@export What is the last day to renew my Consumer and Commercial Division proceedings because the order in my favour was not complied with (Schedule 4 clause 8(2))?
GIVEN `the last day of the period for compliance` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period NCAT gave for complying with the order
GIVETH A DATE
`The last day to renew` MEANS `the last day of the period for compliance` `plus months` 12

GIVEN `the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NCAT party` `NCAT act`
`Sch 4 cl 8(2) -- a renewal notice must be lodged within 12 months after the end of the period` `the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the party`
    MUST `lodge a notice renewing the proceedings`
    WITHIN `the last day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the party` BECAUSE "renewal notice not lodged within 12 months after the end of the period for compliance (Sch 4 cl 8(2))"

@export The order NCAT made in my favour in the Consumer and Commercial Division was not complied with: can I renew the proceedings (Schedule 4 clause 8)?
GIVEN `the order was made in the Consumer and Commercial Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order in your favour was made in NCAT's Consumer and Commercial Division
      `the Tribunal gave me leave to renew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT, when making the order or later, gave you leave to renew the proceedings if the order was not complied with
      `the order was complied with in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order was complied with within the period NCAT specified
      `the order was suspended or appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the operation of the order has been suspended, or the order is or has been the subject of an internal appeal
      `the last day of the period for compliance` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period NCAT gave for complying with the order
      `the day I lodge my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge (or lodged) your notice that the order has not been complied with
GIVETH A `My renewal`
`Can I renew my proceedings` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the order was made in the Consumer and Commercial Division`)
    THEN `clause 8 applies only to orders in the Consumer and Commercial Division`
    ELSE IF `the order was suspended or appealed`
         THEN `clause 8 does not apply: the order's operation was suspended, or it is or has been under internal appeal`
         ELSE IF (NOT `the Tribunal gave me leave to renew`)
              THEN `clause 8 does not apply: the Tribunal has not given me leave to renew`
              ELSE IF `the order was complied with in time`
                   THEN `clause 8 does not apply: the order was complied with in time`
                   ELSE IF (NOT (`the day I lodge my notice` `is after` `the last day of the period for compliance`))
                        THEN `not yet: the period the Tribunal gave for compliance has not ended`
                        ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`Sch 4 cl 8(2) -- a renewal notice must be lodged within 12 months after the end of the period` `the last day`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day lodged`), (EVENT `the party` `lodge a notice renewing the proceedings` `the day lodged`))
                             WHEN FULFILLED THEN `I may renew the proceedings by lodging the notice; it is treated as a new application`
                             OTHERWISE `the 12 months after the end of the compliance period have passed`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (`The last day to renew` `the last day of the period for compliance`)
        `the day lodged` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day I lodge my notice`

-- s 72(1) "A person must not, without lawful excuse, contravene a designated order of the Tribunal. Maximum penalty--
-- (a) in the case of a corporation--100 penalty units, or (b) in any other case--50 penalty units or imprisonment for 12
-- months, or both." (2) designated orders: s 64 non-disclosure orders, Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 s 108(2)(b)-(e) and
-- interim orders, Guardianship Act 1987 s 42 orders, and orders declared designated. The dollar value of a penalty unit
-- is set by the Crimes (Sentencing Procedure) Act 1999 s 17 (not deposited): the answer is in penalty units. With a
-- lawful excuse there is no contravention: 0 (fork F8).
@export What is the largest fine, in penalty units, I can face for contravening a designated NCAT order such as a non-publication order (s 72(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the order is a designated order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order is a "designated order": an order restricting disclosure or publication under s 64, an Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 order under s 108(2)(b)-(e) or interim order, a Guardianship Act 1987 s 42 order, or an order another Act declares designated
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a lawful excuse for not complying (a court decides; answer as you expect it to)
      `I am a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a corporation rather than an individual
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The largest fine for contravening a designated order` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the order is a designated order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 72(1) speaks only of designated orders; see s 72(3))
    ELSE IF `I had a lawful excuse`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE IF `I am a corporation`
              THEN JUST 100
              ELSE JUST 50

@export What is the longest imprisonment, in months, I can face for contravening a designated NCAT order (s 72(1))?
GIVEN `the order is a designated order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order is a "designated order": an order restricting disclosure or publication under s 64, an Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 order under s 108(2)(b)-(e) or interim order, a Guardianship Act 1987 s 42 order, or an order another Act declares designated
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a lawful excuse for not complying (a court decides; answer as you expect it to)
      `I am a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a corporation rather than an individual
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The longest imprisonment for contravening a designated order` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the order is a designated order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 72(1) speaks only of designated orders)
    ELSE IF `I had a lawful excuse` OR `I am a corporation`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE JUST 12

-- s 72(3) "A person must not, without reasonable excuse, contravene any other order of the Tribunal made under this Act or
-- any other legislation. Civil penalty provision." s 77(3) "The monetary penalty must not exceed-- (a) in the case of a
-- contravention by a corporation--$22,000, or (b) in any other case--$11,000." Proceedings are brought only by an
-- authorised official (s 75). A designated order falls under s 72(1), not "any other order": NOTHING (fork F8).
@export What is the largest civil penalty, in dollars, I can be ordered to pay for contravening an ordinary NCAT order (ss 72(3), 77(3))?
GIVEN `the order is a designated order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order is a "designated order" (a non-disclosure order under s 64, certain Anti-Discrimination Act and Guardianship Act orders); answer no for ordinary orders, such as an order to pay money or do work
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a reasonable excuse for not complying (NCAT decides; answer as you expect it to)
      `I am a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a corporation rather than an individual
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The largest civil penalty for contravening an order` MEANS
    IF `the order is a designated order`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (case by case, "(other than X)": s 72(3) covers "any other order"; s 72(1) governs designated orders)
    ELSE IF `I had a reasonable excuse`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE IF `I am a corporation`
              THEN JUST 22000
              ELSE JUST 11000

-- s 76(2) "Proceedings for an offence against this Act may be brought within the period of 12 months of the date on
-- which the offence is alleged to have been committed." s 77(5) "Proceedings for a penalty under this section may be
-- brought within the period of 2 years of the date on which the contravention is alleged to have occurred." Counted as
-- 12 and 24 months after that date (fork F2).
@export What is the last day on which proceedings can be brought against me for contravening an NCAT order (ss 76(2), 77(5))?
GIVEN `the order is a designated order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order is a "designated order" (an offence under s 72(1)); answer no for an ordinary order (a civil penalty under s 72(3))
      `the day of the alleged contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day on which you are alleged to have contravened the order
GIVETH A DATE
`The last day for proceedings about a contravention` MEANS
    IF `the order is a designated order`
    THEN `the day of the alleged contravention` `plus months` 12
    ELSE `the day of the alleged contravention` `plus months` 24

§§ `Part 6 -- appeals`

-- s 32(1) internal appeal jurisdiction covers "(a) any decision made by the Tribunal in proceedings for a general
-- decision or administrative review decision, and (b) any decision made by a registrar of a kind that is declared ... to
-- be internally appealable"; (3) it "does not extend to" a decision of an Appeal Panel, a decision in an external appeal,
-- in enforcement proceedings, or imposing a civil penalty in the general jurisdiction. s 80(1): an appeal "may be made to
-- an Appeal Panel by a party to the proceedings in which the decision is made". (2) "(a) in the case of an interlocutory
-- decision ...--with the leave of the Appeal Panel, and (b) in the case of any other kind of decision (including an
-- ancillary decision) ...--as of right on any question of law, or with the leave of the Appeal Panel, on any other
-- grounds." The Division Schedules: Sch 3 cl 15 (not internally appealable: Working with Children, NDIS worker check,
-- lands legislation, Native Title Part 7, Plant Diseases s 21, Victims Rights and Support Act s 51 review, and
-- Anti-Discrimination Act s 96 leave decisions); Sch 3 cl 16 (Anti-Discrimination Act interim orders: leave only, "even
-- if it is on a question of law"); Sch 5 cl 29(1) (profession decisions: not internally appealable); Sch 4 cl 12(2)
-- (question of law only, "not on any other grounds (even with leave)", for a corporation's credit dispute appeal and a
-- tenancy termination order executed by a warrant of possession); Sch 6 cl 12(4) (an appeal to the Supreme Court
-- precludes an internal appeal unless withdrawn with the Court's approval). Every bar is a flat "not" or "only": the
-- answer says no.
@export Can I appeal to NCAT's Appeal Panel against the decision, and do I need leave (ss 32, 80 and the Division Schedules)?
GIVEN `I was a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a party to the proceedings in which the decision was made
      `who made the decision` IS A `Who made the decision` @desc Who made the decision and in what proceedings. One of: "the Tribunal at first instance, in a general or administrative review matter", "the Tribunal imposing a civil penalty in its general jurisdiction", "a registrar, in a kind of decision declared internally appealable", "a registrar, in any other kind of decision", "an Appeal Panel", "the Tribunal in an external appeal", "the Tribunal in contempt or civil penalty enforcement proceedings under this Act"
      `the kind of decision` IS A `Kind of decision` @desc What kind of decision it is. One of: "an interlocutory decision" (an adjournment, stay, summons, extension of time, evidence, joinder, summary dismissal, leave to be represented and similar), "a decision as to costs", "a decision made with the consent of the parties", "any other decision, ancillary or final"
      `my ground` IS A `My ground of appeal` @desc Your ground of appeal. One of: "a question of law", "other grounds (fact, or fact and law)"
      `the special kind` IS A `Special kind of decision` @desc Whether the decision is one of the kinds the Division Schedules treat specially; otherwise "none of the special kinds". One of: "none of the special kinds", "a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision", "a decision under the lands legislation", "a Native Title (New South Wales) Act 1994 Part 7 determination", "a Plant Diseases Act 1924 s 21 administrative review decision", "a victims support administrative review decision under Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 51", "a decision on leave under Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 s 96", "an interim order under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1977", "a profession decision of the Occupational Division (Schedule 5 clause 29(1))", "a Consumer and Commercial credit dispute decision, appealed by a corporation (Credit (Commonwealth Powers) Act 2010 Sch 3)", "a tenancy termination order under which a warrant of possession has been executed", "a Guardianship Division decision I have already appealed to the Supreme Court"
GIVETH A `My internal appeal`
`Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I was a party to the proceedings`)
    THEN `only a party to the proceedings in which the decision was made may appeal`
    ELSE IF `outside the internal appeal jurisdiction`
         THEN `no internal appeal lies against this decision`
         ELSE IF `made not internally appealable by a Division Schedule`
              THEN `no internal appeal lies against this decision`
              ELSE IF `the kind of decision` EQUALS `an interlocutory decision` OR `the special kind` EQUALS `an interim order under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1977`
                   THEN `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel only with its leave`
                   ELSE IF    `the special kind` EQUALS `a Consumer and Commercial credit dispute decision, appealed by a corporation (Credit (Commonwealth Powers) Act 2010 Sch 3)`
                           OR `the special kind` EQUALS `a tenancy termination order under which a warrant of possession has been executed`
                        THEN `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel on a question of law only, as of right, and not on other grounds even with leave`
                        ELSE IF `my ground` EQUALS `a question of law`
                             THEN `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel as of right`
                             ELSE `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel only with its leave`
    WHERE
        `outside the internal appeal jurisdiction` MEANS
               `who made the decision` EQUALS `the Tribunal imposing a civil penalty in its general jurisdiction`
            OR `who made the decision` EQUALS `a registrar, in any other kind of decision`
            OR `who made the decision` EQUALS `an Appeal Panel`
            OR `who made the decision` EQUALS `the Tribunal in an external appeal`
            OR `who made the decision` EQUALS `the Tribunal in contempt or civil penalty enforcement proceedings under this Act`
        `made not internally appealable by a Division Schedule` MEANS
               `the special kind` EQUALS `a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision`
            OR `the special kind` EQUALS `a decision under the lands legislation`
            OR `the special kind` EQUALS `a Native Title (New South Wales) Act 1994 Part 7 determination`
            OR `the special kind` EQUALS `a Plant Diseases Act 1924 s 21 administrative review decision`
            OR `the special kind` EQUALS `a victims support administrative review decision under Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 51`
            OR `the special kind` EQUALS `a decision on leave under Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 s 96`
            OR `the special kind` EQUALS `a profession decision of the Occupational Division (Schedule 5 clause 29(1))`
            OR `the special kind` EQUALS `a Guardianship Division decision I have already appealed to the Supreme Court`

DECLARE `Miscarriage reason` IS ONE OF
    `the decision was not fair and equitable`
    `the decision was against the weight of evidence`
    `significant new evidence has arisen that was not reasonably available when the proceedings were dealt with`
    `some other reason`

-- Sch 4 cl 12(1) "An Appeal Panel may grant leave under section 80(2)(b) ... for an internal appeal against a Division
-- decision only if the Appeal Panel is satisfied the appellant may have suffered a substantial miscarriage of justice
-- because-- (a) the decision ... was not fair and equitable, or (b) ... was against the weight of evidence, or (c)
-- significant new evidence has arisen (being evidence that was not reasonably available at the time ...)." "only if":
-- JUST FALSE when it fails. Outside the Consumer and Commercial Division the Act sets no test for leave (NOTHING).
@export In the Consumer and Commercial Division, can the Appeal Panel give me leave to appeal on grounds other than a question of law (Schedule 4 clause 12(1))?
GIVEN `the decision was made in the Consumer and Commercial Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision you want to appeal was made in NCAT's Consumer and Commercial Division
      `the Appeal Panel is satisfied I may have suffered a substantial miscarriage of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Appeal Panel is satisfied you may have suffered a substantial miscarriage of justice (it decides; answer as you expect it to)
      `the reason` IS A `Miscarriage reason` @desc Why. One of: "the decision was not fair and equitable", "the decision was against the weight of evidence", "significant new evidence has arisen that was not reasonably available when the proceedings were dealt with", "some other reason"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Appeal Panel give me leave` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the decision was made in the Consumer and Commercial Division`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: the Act sets a test for leave only in Sch 4 cl 12(1))
    ELSE IF `the Appeal Panel is satisfied I may have suffered a substantial miscarriage of justice` AND (NOT (`the reason` EQUALS `some other reason`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 82(1) appealable decisions: an Appeal Panel's decision in an internal appeal, the Tribunal's decision in an external
-- appeal, a decision in proceedings imposing a civil penalty; (2) not a contempt decision, nor an Appeal Panel's decision
-- in an internal appeal from a registrar. (3) civil penalty appeals go to the Supreme Court if the Tribunal included a
-- senior judicial officer, otherwise to the District Court. s 83(1) "A party to an external or internal appeal may, with
-- the leave of the Supreme Court, appeal on a question of law ...". (2) "A person on whom a civil penalty has been imposed
-- ... may appeal to the appropriate appeal court ... on a question of law". Division Schedules: Sch 3 cl 17 (Working with
-- Children and NDIS worker check: Supreme Court, question of law), cl 18 (lands legislation: Land and Environment Court);
-- Sch 5 cl 29(2), (4), (6) (profession decisions: Supreme Court; Legal Profession Uniform Law appeals by rehearing; others
-- as of right on law or with leave on other grounds; interlocutory, consent and costs decisions only with leave); Sch 6
-- cl 12, 14(1) (Guardianship: Supreme Court as of right on law or with leave on other grounds; interlocutory with leave;
-- an internal appeal precludes it unless withdrawn with approval). Out: Sch 5 cl 29(2)(a), (3) (Aboriginal Land Rights
-- vacancy orders and Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act s 89(2) decisions).
-- Sch 3 cl 15(a), (e)-(g) take some decisions out of the internal appeal jurisdiction and no provision of the Act gives
-- an appeal to a court against them (they are not "appealable decisions" under s 82(1)): no appeal under this Act.
@export Can I appeal to a court against the NCAT decision, to which court, and on what grounds (ss 82, 83 and the Division Schedules)?
GIVEN `I was a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a party to the proceedings (or the person on whom the civil penalty was imposed)
      `the decision` IS A `Decision for a court appeal` @desc Which decision you want to appeal. One of: "a decision of an Appeal Panel in an internal appeal from the Tribunal", "a decision of an Appeal Panel in an internal appeal from a registrar", "a decision of the Tribunal in an external appeal", "a decision in proceedings in which a civil penalty was imposed on me", "a decision in proceedings for contempt of the Tribunal", "a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division", "a lands legislation decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division", "a profession decision of the Occupational Division under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (NSW)", "any other profession decision of the Occupational Division", "an internally appealable decision of the Tribunal in the Guardianship Division", "a decision Schedule 3 clause 15 makes not internally appealable, with no court appeal given (victims support s 51 review, Native Title Part 7, Plant Diseases s 21, Anti-Discrimination Act s 96 leave)", "any other decision of the Tribunal at first instance"
      `the kind of decision` IS A `Kind of decision` @desc What kind of decision it is. One of: "an interlocutory decision", "a decision as to costs", "a decision made with the consent of the parties", "any other decision, ancillary or final"
      `my ground` IS A `My ground of appeal` @desc Your ground of appeal. One of: "a question of law", "other grounds (fact, or fact and law)"
      `the Tribunal that imposed the penalty included a senior judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a civil penalty: whether NCAT was constituted by or with a Judge of the District Court, Land and Environment Court or Supreme Court, or a judicial member of the Industrial Relations Commission
      `I have a Guardianship internal appeal not withdrawn with approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Guardianship Division decision: whether you have lodged an internal appeal against the same decision that has not been withdrawn with the Appeal Panel's approval
GIVETH A `My court appeal`
`Can I appeal to a court` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I was a party to the proceedings`)
    THEN `only a party to the proceedings may appeal`
    ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `a decision of an Appeal Panel in an internal appeal from the Tribunal` OR `the decision` EQUALS `a decision of the Tribunal in an external appeal`
         THEN `on a question of law only` `to the Supreme Court, with its leave, on a question of law only`
         ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `a decision of an Appeal Panel in an internal appeal from a registrar` OR `the decision` EQUALS `a decision Schedule 3 clause 15 makes not internally appealable, with no court appeal given (victims support s 51 review, Native Title Part 7, Plant Diseases s 21, Anti-Discrimination Act s 96 leave)`
              THEN `no appeal to a court lies under this Act against this decision`
              ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `a decision in proceedings in which a civil penalty was imposed on me`
                   THEN IF `the Tribunal that imposed the penalty included a senior judicial officer`
                        THEN `on a question of law only` `to the Supreme Court, as of right, on a question of law`
                        ELSE `on a question of law only` `to the District Court, as of right, on a question of law`
                   ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `a decision in proceedings for contempt of the Tribunal`
                        THEN `not under Part 6: a contempt decision is appealed under District Court Act 1973 s 201, as applied by section 73`
                        ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division`
                             THEN `on a question of law only` `to the Supreme Court, as of right, on a question of law`
                             ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `a lands legislation decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division`
                                  THEN `to the Land and Environment Court`
                                  ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `a profession decision of the Occupational Division under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (NSW)`
                                       THEN IF `needs leave under Schedule 5 clause 29(6)`
                                            THEN `to the Supreme Court, only with its leave`
                                            ELSE `to the Supreme Court, by way of rehearing`
                                       ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `any other profession decision of the Occupational Division`
                                            THEN IF `needs leave under Schedule 5 clause 29(6)`
                                                 THEN `to the Supreme Court, only with its leave`
                                                 ELSE `to the Supreme Court, as of right on a question of law, or with its leave on other grounds`
                                            ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `an internally appealable decision of the Tribunal in the Guardianship Division`
                                                 THEN IF `I have a Guardianship internal appeal not withdrawn with approval`
                                                      THEN `not while my internal appeal stands, unless it is withdrawn with the Appeal Panel's approval`
                                                      ELSE IF `the kind of decision` EQUALS `an interlocutory decision`
                                                           THEN `to the Supreme Court, only with its leave`
                                                           ELSE `to the Supreme Court, as of right on a question of law, or with its leave on other grounds`
                                                 ELSE `not to a court under this Act: the decision goes first to an internal appeal`
    WHERE
        `needs leave under Schedule 5 clause 29(6)` MEANS
               `the kind of decision` EQUALS `an interlocutory decision`
            OR `the kind of decision` EQUALS `a decision as to costs`
            OR `the kind of decision` EQUALS `a decision made with the consent of the parties`
        `on a question of law only` `the answer` MEANS
            IF `my ground` EQUALS `a question of law`
            THEN `the answer`
            ELSE `not on that ground: the appeal lies on a question of law only`

-- s 84(2) "An appeal ... must be made-- (a) within such time and in such manner as is prescribed by the rules of court ...,
-- or (b) within such further time as the court may allow." The Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 2005 are not deposited: the
-- last day is asked. Sch 6 cl 14(2): an appeal from the Guardianship Division "is to be instituted-- (a) in the case of an
-- ancillary or interlocutory decision ...--within the period ending 28 days after the relevant decision has been made, or
-- (b) in any other case--within the period ending 28 days after the day on which the written statement of reasons ... is
-- given to the person seeking to appeal, or (c) within such further time as the Supreme Court may, in any case, allow."
@export What is the last day to appeal to the Supreme Court against a Guardianship Division decision (Schedule 6 clause 14(2))?
GIVEN `the decision is ancillary or interlocutory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is an ancillary or interlocutory decision (rather than the decision determining the application)
      `the day the decision was made` IS A DATE @desc The day NCAT made the decision
      `the day I was given the written reasons` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given NCAT's written statement of reasons for the decision (any date, if the decision is ancillary or interlocutory)
GIVETH A DATE
`The last day for my guardianship appeal` MEANS
    IF `the decision is ancillary or interlocutory`
    THEN `the day the decision was made` `plus days` 28
    ELSE `the day I was given the written reasons` `plus days` 28

GIVEN `the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NCAT party` `NCAT act`
`s 84(2), Sch 6 cl 14(2) -- an appeal to a court must be instituted in time` `the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the party`
    MUST `institute the appeal to the court`
    WITHIN `the last day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the party` BECAUSE "appeal to the court not instituted within the time fixed, or any further time the court allowed (s 84(2), Sch 6 cl 14(2))"

@export Is my appeal to a court against the NCAT decision in time (s 84(2), Schedule 6 clause 14(2))?
GIVEN `the appeal is from the Guardianship Division to the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your appeal is to the Supreme Court from a Guardianship Division decision under Schedule 6
      `the decision is ancillary or interlocutory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Guardianship appeal: whether the decision is an ancillary or interlocutory decision
      `the day the decision was made` IS A DATE @desc For a Guardianship appeal: the day NCAT made the decision
      `the day I was given the written reasons` IS A DATE @desc For a Guardianship appeal: the day you were given the written statement of reasons
      `the last day under the rules of court` IS A DATE @desc For any other appeal: the last day for appealing that the court's rules (the Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 2005) set
      `the court has allowed further time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has allowed you further time to appeal
      `the last day of the further time` IS A DATE @desc If the court allowed further time, the last day of it (otherwise any date)
      `the day I institute the appeal` IS A DATE @desc The day you institute (or instituted) your appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my court appeal in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 84(2), Sch 6 cl 14(2) -- an appeal to a court must be instituted in time` `the last day`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day instituted`), (EVENT `the party` `institute the appeal to the court` `the day instituted`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `the court has allowed further time`
            THEN DATE_SERIAL `the last day of the further time`
            ELSE IF `the appeal is from the Guardianship Division to the Supreme Court`
                 THEN DATE_SERIAL (`The last day for my guardianship appeal` `the decision is ancillary or interlocutory` `the day the decision was made` `the day I was given the written reasons`)
                 ELSE DATE_SERIAL `the last day under the rules of court`
        `the day instituted` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day I institute the appeal`

§§ `Schedule 4 clause 5 -- the Tribunal and the courts (Consumer and Commercial Division)`

-- Sch 4 cl 5(3) "If, at the time when an application was made to the Tribunal for the exercise of a Division function, no
-- issue arising under the application was the subject of a dispute in proceedings pending before a court, a court has no
-- jurisdiction to hear or determine such an issue." (4) this "ceases to apply to the extent to which the application
-- concerned is dismissed for want of jurisdiction or withdrawn". (5) it does not prevent a court hearing a claim that a
-- Tribunal order "is invalid for want of jurisdiction". (6) an issue arises under the application "only if the existence
-- of the issue is shown in the applicant's claim or is recorded in the record made by the Tribunal". (1), (2) "court"
-- includes any tribunal, arbitrator or body that can decide the dispute, but not a body that can only discipline, the
-- Ombudsman, or a body whose decisions bind only one party. A flat "has no jurisdiction": JUST FALSE. Where the bar does
-- not apply, the court's own jurisdiction decides (NOTHING). The clause reads the pending-proceedings test per issue
-- (fork F9).
@export Can a court decide an issue that is part of my Consumer and Commercial Division application to NCAT (Schedule 4 clause 5(3)-(6))?
GIVEN `my application is in the Consumer and Commercial Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application to NCAT is in its Consumer and Commercial Division
      `the other body is a court for clause 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other body is a court, tribunal, arbitrator or other body able to decide the dispute (answer no for the Ombudsman, a body that can only discipline and cannot award compensation, or a body whose decisions bind only one party)
      `the issue is shown in my claim or recorded by the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the issue is shown in your claim to NCAT or recorded in NCAT's record of the proceedings
      `the issue was already before that court when I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you applied to NCAT, the issue was already in dispute in proceedings pending before that court
      `my application was dismissed for want of jurisdiction or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your NCAT application, so far as it raises the issue, has been dismissed for want of jurisdiction or withdrawn
      `the court claim is that a Tribunal order is invalid for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court proceedings claim that an NCAT order or decision is invalid because NCAT had no jurisdiction
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can a court decide my Tribunal issue` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`my application is in the Consumer and Commercial Division` AND `the other body is a court for clause 5`))
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: cl 5 speaks only of Consumer and Commercial applications and "courts")
    ELSE IF `the court claim is that a Tribunal order is invalid for want of jurisdiction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF    (NOT `the issue is shown in my claim or recorded by the Tribunal`)
                 OR `the issue was already before that court when I applied`
                 OR `my application was dismissed for want of jurisdiction or withdrawn`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (grant limited in its own wording: the cl 5(3) bar does not reach this case; the court's own jurisdiction decides)
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Sch 4 cl 5(7) "If, at the time when an application is made to the Tribunal ..., an issue arising under the application
-- was the subject of a dispute in proceedings pending before a court, the Tribunal, on becoming aware of those
-- proceedings, ceases to have jurisdiction to hear or determine the issue." (8) this "ceases to apply to the extent to
-- which the proceedings concerned are dismissed or quashed ... for want of jurisdiction or without deciding the issue on
-- its merits, or withdrawn". Taken once the Tribunal is aware of the court proceedings (fork F9).
@export Can NCAT decide an issue in my Consumer and Commercial Division application that was already before a court when I applied (Schedule 4 clause 5(7), (8))?
GIVEN `my application is in the Consumer and Commercial Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application to NCAT is in its Consumer and Commercial Division
      `the other body is a court for clause 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other body is a court, tribunal, arbitrator or other body able to decide the dispute (answer no for the Ombudsman, a body that can only discipline and cannot award compensation, or a body whose decisions bind only one party)
      `the issue was already before that court when I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you applied to NCAT, the issue was already in dispute in proceedings pending before that court
      `those court proceedings ended without deciding the issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those court proceedings have been dismissed or quashed for want of jurisdiction or without deciding the issue on its merits, or withdrawn
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal decide an issue already in court` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`my application is in the Consumer and Commercial Division` AND `the other body is a court for clause 5`))
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: cl 5 speaks only of Consumer and Commercial applications and "courts")
    ELSE IF (NOT `the issue was already before that court when I applied`) OR `those court proceedings ended without deciding the issue`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (grant limited in its own wording: the cl 5(7) bar does not reach this case)
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 71 and Schedule 3 clause 13B -- giving information and evidence`

-- s 71 "A person must not, in any proceedings or application to the Tribunal, provide any information, or make any
-- statement, to the Tribunal knowing that the information or statement is false or misleading in a material respect.
-- Maximum penalty--50 penalty units or imprisonment for 12 months, or both." The same maximum for a corporation (no
-- separate figure). Without knowledge, or where the falsity is not material, the offence is not made out: 0 (fork F8).
@export What is the largest fine, in penalty units, for giving NCAT information I know is false or misleading (s 71)? Up to 12 months' imprisonment may be imposed as well.
GIVEN `I knew it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew, when you gave it, that the information or statement was false or misleading
      `it was false or misleading in a material respect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information or statement was false or misleading in a way that matters to the proceedings, not just a trivial slip
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The largest fine for a false statement to the Tribunal` MEANS
    IF `I knew it was false or misleading` AND `it was false or misleading in a material respect`
    THEN 50
    ELSE 0

-- Sch 3 cl 13B "Despite section 46 of this Act, the Tribunal may not compel a witness to give evidence or produce
-- documents in review proceedings under Part 5 of the Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 if the witness is the victim of
-- the relevant offence (within the meaning of that Part) to which the review proceedings relate." Part 5 of that Act is
-- the recovery of victims support from offenders (restitution), so these are usually an offender's review. A flat "may
-- not": JUST FALSE. Otherwise s 46 lets the Tribunal compel a witness subject to a reasonable excuse (s 46(3)): NOTHING.
@export If the offender seeks review of a restitution order under Part 5 of the Victims Rights and Support Act 2013, can NCAT compel me, the victim, to give evidence or produce documents (Schedule 3 clause 13B)?
GIVEN `the proceedings are a review under Part 5 of the Victims Rights and Support Act 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the NCAT proceedings are a review under Part 5 of the Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 (recovery of victims support from an offender)
      `I am the victim of the relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the victim of the offence to which those review proceedings relate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be compelled to give evidence in the restitution review` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are a review under Part 5 of the Victims Rights and Support Act 2013` AND `I am the victim of the relevant offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: cl 13B speaks only of the victim in Part 5 reviews; s 46 leaves it to the Tribunal)
